{:edb/db-before-t 1653 :edb/db-after-t 1654 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534966 50 #inst "2026-10-08T12:24:05.357Z" 13194139534966 true] [17592186105669 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323234 13194139534966 true] [17592186105669 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323241 13194139534966 true] [17592186105670 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323220 13194139534966 true] [17592186105670 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323227 13194139534966 true] [17592186105670 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323248 13194139534966 true] [17592186323220 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323221 13194139534966 true] [17592186323220 1089 "q-130924" 13194139534966 true] [17592186323220 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534966 true] [17592186323220 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+8y=4 \\\\ -3x+12y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139534966 true] [17592186323220 1113 #uuid "525c9b4e-5061-5f7f-a265-ef8373526104" 13194139534966 true] [17592186323220 1145 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 10 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 8 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-4y=-2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-4y=-2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=4y-2,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4y-2 \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y-2 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534966 true] [17592186323221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323222 13194139534966 true] [17592186323221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323223 13194139534966 true] [17592186323221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323224 13194139534966 true] [17592186323221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323225 13194139534966 true] [17592186323221 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323226 13194139534966 true] [17592186323221 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534966 true] [17592186323221 1041 "selection" 13194139534966 true] [17592186323221 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323226 13194139534966 true] [17592186323221 1110 #uuid "78ba4fc7-81a4-5c27-93ef-128c34f84c5f" 13194139534966 true] [17592186323222 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2y-4 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534966 true] [17592186323222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534966 true] [17592186323222 1111 #uuid "39a51199-99ce-5199-8ae8-086b23e9b326" 13194139534966 true] [17592186323223 1034 "No solution" 13194139534966 true] [17592186323223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534966 true] [17592186323223 1111 #uuid "dda85ba0-d567-5719-aede-35151e674082" 13194139534966 true] [17592186323224 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y+2 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139534966 true] [17592186323224 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534966 true] [17592186323224 1111 #uuid "a41ea055-be2d-5866-bc27-5eab17639e72" 13194139534966 true] [17592186323225 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-4y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 131941395